> such as:
>
> a- 4 daggers
>
> right?

Correct.  Nethack uses the word stack carefully this way.
Certain items like daggers stack.  Certain items like long
swords don't stack.  Stack is only for the ones that merge
into a single inventory letter when you pick them up.

> When the article refers to the 'pile', i'm assuming this is the
> collection of all items on a particular square?
>
> a- 4 daggers
> b- potion of oil
> c- flail

That is what the document means.  Since the word stack
is reserved, a different word was needed.  Even though
stack and pile mean much the same thing in normal
usage a technical distinction was needed.

> assuming i have this part correct, i should be able to work out the
> optimal amounts of gear to poly at once.

If I read the document correctly the optimal amount of
items is "more" if what you want to do is increase variety
of item types you have encountered.  In much practice
issues like which items are magical or not make
non-magical items far less important at times.

